<title>HONG KONG: China firm wins HK$174.7 mln HK airport contract.</title>
<headline>China firm wins HK$174.7 mln HK airport contract.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Airport Authority said in a statement it awarded on Friday a HK$174.7 million contract to Chinese state-owned China State Construction Engineering Corp for works in the territory's new airport.</p>
<p>The deal involves the construction of land-based sea rescue facilities at four locations around the perimeter of the airport platform, the authority said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
